{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan-review remediation for 4144-2784-6437-4efb (tireless-ruinable-prairiedog)\nInvestigated read-only in the worktree /Users/joeoakhart/impl-2ddd-consolidation\non 2026-08-21, at HEAD 3406014085.\n\n================================================================================\nWHAT WAS FACTUALLY WRONG, AND WHAT REPLACED IT\n================================================================================\n\n1. NON-EXISTENT TEST PATH.\n   Plan cited tests/unit/llm/code_review/test_criteria_routing.py and an AC of\n   `pytest tests/unit/llm/code_review -k routing`.\n   There is no tests/unit/llm/ directory at all.\n     COMMAND: ls tests/unit/llm/code_review/\n     OUTPUT:  ls: tests/unit/llm/code_review/: No such file or directory\n     COMMAND: .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/llm/code_review -k routing -q\n     OUTPUT:  ERROR: file or directory not found: tests/unit/llm/code_review\n              no tests ran in 0.07s\n   Code-review tests live flat, as tests/unit/test_code_review_*.py (e.g.\n   test_code_review_ws5.py, test_code_review_nit_routing.py,\n   test_code_review_blocking_replay.py). Corrected to a new\n   tests/unit/test_code_review_criteria_routing.py.\n\n2. NON-EXISTENT CHECKER.\n   Plan cited `scripts/check_criteria_routing_parity`.\n     COMMAND: ls scripts/check_criteria_routing_parity*\n     OUTPUT:  zsh: no matches found\n     COMMAND: ls scripts/ | grep -i \"parity|routing\"\n     OUTPUT:  check_verify_gate_parity.py    (unrelated)\n   The only criteria-routing parity gate in CI is\n   .github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml:548-560, and reading it shows it covers\n   src/rebar/llm/plan_review/criteria_routing.json ONLY - there is no code-review\n   routing parity gate. Removed the citation; the parity assertion now lives in\n   the new unit test instead.\n\n3. WRONG SCRIPT IN SCOPE.\n   Plan listed \"scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py allowlist if the criterion\n   ids are new to it\".\n     COMMAND: sed -n '1,45p' scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py\n     OUTPUT (line 2):  \"\"\"Check that deprecated ticket vocabulary remains confined\n                          to reviewed records.\"\"\"\n     OUTPUT (lines 21-22):\n       PHRASE_PATTERN = re.compile(r\"\\b\" + \"success\" + r\"[ _-]criteri(?:a|on)\\b\", ...)\n       ABBREVIATION_PATTERN = re.compile(r\"\\bSCs?\\b\")\n   It guards the DEPRECATED TICKET PHRASE \"success criteria\" / \"SC\". It has\n   nothing to do with review-criterion ids. Its allowlist is also a separate file\n   (scripts/criteria-vocabulary-allowlist.txt), not part of the .py. Removed from\n   Scope with the reason recorded.\n\n4. STALE RESOLVER CITATION.\n   Plan cited \"unknown criteria default to 0.95/off,\n   src/rebar/llm/code_review/registry.py:496-497\".\n   Lines 496-501 are DOCSTRING PROSE. The implementation delegates:\n     registry.py:513-514   idx = routing_map if ... else routing_index()\n                           return _criteria.threshold_for(criteria, idx, gate=_GATE_KEY)\n     registry.py:26        from rebar.llm import criteria as _criteria\n     registry.py:29        _GATE_KEY = \"code_review\"\n   The real resolution is src/rebar/llm/criteria/model.py:45-88, which reads\n   block_threshold (min over criteria, default DEFAULT_BLOCK_THRESHOLD) and, for\n   gate==\"code_review\", blocking_enabled. The constant is registry.py:148\n   (DEFAULT_BLOCK_THRESHOLD = 0.95). Corrected all three citations.\n\n5. WRONG SCHEMA FIELD NAMES.\n   Plan wrote \"(exec AGENT, posture advisory, threshold 0.95)\".\n     COMMAND: python3 -c \"json.load(...); print sorted key union\"\n     OUTPUT:  ['_comment','applies_to','block_threshold','blocking_enabled',\n               'default_posture','detector','exec','fail_mode','nit_suppressed']\n   The keys are default_posture and block_threshold. A literal entry, for shape:\n     \"concurrency\": {\"exec\":\"AGENT\",\"applies_to\":[],\"default_posture\":\"advisory\",\n                     \"block_threshold\":0.95,\"blocking_enabled\":false}\n   Corrected throughout.\n\n6. THE APPROACH AS WRITTEN WOULD HAVE BEEN PARTLY INERT.\n   correctness and edge-cases are BASE-REVIEWER dimensions, not overlays.\n     COMMAND: grep -n \"edge-cases\" over src/\n     OUTPUT:  src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code-review-base.md:34 - the base reviewer's\n              evidence-record contract lists `correctness`, `edge-cases`,\n              `error-handling`, `maintainability`, `regression` as the dimension ids\n     COMMAND: sed -n '38,54p' src/rebar/llm/code_review/registry.py\n     OUTPUT:  OVERLAY_IDS is a closed 16-tuple: security, performance, i18n, a11y,\n              db-migrations, docs, supply-chain, api-compat, iac, tests,\n              llm-prompts, deletion-impact, concurrency, scope-intent,\n              surface-parity  -- neither correctness nor edge-cases is a member.\n   The already-shipped `regression` entry documents the consequence in its own\n   _comment (criteria_routing.json:159-160): for a base-reviewer dimension\n   \"exec/applies_to are inert here and only the posture/threshold/blocking_enabled\n   fields are consulted by registry.threshold_for\".\n   So the plan's \"exec AGENT\" does nothing. Corrected: the new rows are authored\n   as base-reviewer rows in the regression shape, and the plan now says plainly\n   that only default_posture / block_threshold / blocking_enabled are operative.\n\n   Confirmed the two ids are genuinely absent today:\n     COMMAND: python3 -c \"... print('HAS correctness:', 'correctness' in d,\n                          '| HAS edge-cases:', 'edge-cases' in d)\"\n     OUTPUT:  HAS correctness: False | HAS edge-cases: False\n   And the 21 present keys are: security, performance, i18n, a11y, db-migrations,\n   docs, supply-chain, api-compat, iac, tests, llm-prompts, deletion-impact,\n   scope-intent, concurrency, regression, error-handling, surface-parity,\n   secret-detection, high-critical-security, public-exposure-without-auth,\n   conflict-markers.\n   Current postures confirmed: tests 0.54/blocking, regression 0.54/blocking,\n   concurrency 0.95/advisory (criteria_routing.json:110-118, :159-166, :151-158).\n\n7. UNPRODUCIBLE METRIC.\n   AC 2 required \"amended-after count\" per criterion. No committed tool computes\n   it.\n     COMMAND: grep -n \"amended|would.block|percent|print(\" \\\n                docs/experiments/calibrate_code_review_thresholds.py\n     OUTPUT:  no \"amended\" hit anywhere; the emitted columns are the ones in\n              docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration.md:80 ->\n              criterion | thr | surviving | would-block | of surviving |\n              changes hit | of all changes | mean validity | val<0.5\n   Dropped the metric; the plan now records exactly the columns the tool emits.\n\n8. WRONG TOOL FOR THE MEASUREMENT.\n   Plan said \"run the existing v4 friction replay ... at 0.54\".\n     COMMAND: grep -n \"add_argument\" docs/experiments/replay_code_v4_would_block.py\n     OUTPUT:  a single --tracker argument (lines 177-183). No per-criterion or\n              per-threshold flag.\n   The script re-applies the PACKAGED posture via threshold_for (:64), so it\n   cannot replay a hypothetical 0.54 for a criterion that is not routed there.\n   The right tool is docs/experiments/calibrate_code_review_thresholds.py, whose\n   pooling is criterion-id-generic:\n     calibrate_code_review_thresholds.py:86   return f.get(\"criteria\") or [\"<none>\"]\n     calibrate_code_review_thresholds.py:99-101  --tracker / --impact-model-version / --emit\n   Corrected: step 2 uses calibrate...py --tracker --emit.\n\n9. MISSING CONSUMER - hard-coded blocking set that would go stale.\n     docs/experiments/replay_code_v4_would_block.py:45-55\n       _BLOCKING_SET = (\"secret-detection\",\"high-critical-security\",\"security\",\n                        \"api-compat\",\"deletion-impact\",\"regression\",\n                        \"error-handling\",\"tests\")\n     docs/experiments/replay_code_v4_would_block.py:106\n       print(f\"  blocking set  : {', '.join(_BLOCKING_SET)}\")\n   The gate it actually applies comes from threshold_for (:64), so any posture\n   flip desynchronises the printed summary from the applied posture. Added the\n   file to Scope and made \"derive it from routing_index()\" an acceptance\n   criterion, which conveniently also fails on the current tree.\n\n10. MISSING CONSUMERS - the canonical vocabulary widens.\n    registry.py:167-171 registers the code-review gate with\n      canonical=lambda: frozenset(routing_index())\n    i.e. the canonical criterion vocabulary IS the routing key set. Adding two\n    keys therefore widens registry.effective_criteria(repo_root). Readers found:\n      COMMAND: grep -rn \"effective_criteria\" --include=\"*.py\" src/ tests/ scripts/\n      src/rebar/llm/evals/eval.py:414-417\n      src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_solver.py:206-211\n      src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py:449-461\n      src/rebar/llm/workflow/criterion_preview.py:551-566\n    That widening is the intended effect (the dimensions become previewable and\n    eval-addressable), so the plan now asserts it rather than leaving it to be\n    discovered by a failing test.\n\n11. MISSING CONSUMER - this repo's own overlay already re-tunes concurrency.\n      COMMAND: python3 -c \"json.load(open('.rebar/criteria_routing.json')) ...\"\n      OUTPUT:  code_review.concurrency = {\"trigger_tokens\":[\".lock\",\"retry\",\n               \"Popen\",\"setsid\",\"fork\",\"stage_and_commit\",\"push_tickets_branch\",\n               \"refs/reconciler/\"], \"applies_to\":[\"**/_store/**\",\"**/lock*\",\n               \"**/enrich_drain*\",\".github/workflows/**\"]}\n    Merge semantics checked at src/rebar/llm/criteria/overlay.py:320-360: an\n    un-prefixed built-in id is a RE-TUNE, \"routing merged over the packaged\n    entry\", field by field. Since the overlay sets neither blocking_enabled nor\n    block_threshold, a packaged flip survives. No overlay edit needed - and the\n    plan now asserts this rather than assuming it.\n\n12. SOURCED THE 8% BUDGET.\n    The plan cited an \"8% friction budget\" with no source. It is not in the\n    calibration document (whose measured table at :74-92 tops out at 2.81% of\n    changes). It is the operator-accepted figure recorded in the tests entry's\n    _comment, criteria_routing.json:110:\n      \"... so the gate can block consequential test-sufficiency findings -\n       blocks 99 changes / 8.0%, operator-accepted ...\"\n    Recorded that provenance in the plan.\n\n13. PORTABILITY / CORPUS AVAILABILITY.\n    replay_code_v4_would_block.py:16-18 states the corpus is NOT committed - it\n    lives in a checkout's .tickets-tracker sidecar store. The plan now says the\n    measurement runs once by the author and only its OUTPUT lands, and every\n    CI-checked criterion is corpus-free and CI-provider-free (project.portability).\n    Confirmed the corpus-free self-check works today:\n      COMMAND: .venv/bin/python docs/experiments/replay_code_v4_would_block.py\n      OUTPUT:  self-check (corpus-free, deterministic):\n                 contract-contradiction fire case : impact=0.9000 block=True\n                 debt-only + hard_to_reverse      : impact=0.2400 block=False\n                 PASS\n               exit=0\n\n================================================================================\nCITED ARTIFACTS - ALL VERIFIED TO EXIST\n================================================================================\n  COMMAND: git log -1 --format=\"%h %s\" <sha>\n    c3aec3eae6  fix: bound completion evidence before banking\n    d2dea317ec  Trigger compaction from the close, out of band\n    61d50b0513  Redesign code-review impact model as code-v4\n  COMMAND: rebar show <id>\n    earthen-flayed-baboon -> 1d71-a76c-04f6-4642  closed  bug\n      \"Completion verifier banks met=false at search exhaustion - should bank\"\n    58bd-d656-c52f-4cf4   -> in_progress  epic  (RP-06, the relates_to link)\n    obese-dihedral-ermine -> 7f9f-05f4-796a-4c63  closed  bug (the tests flip)\n  Files confirmed present:\n    src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json\n    docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration.md\n    docs/experiments/calibrate_code_review_thresholds.py\n    docs/experiments/replay_code_v4_would_block.py\n    docs/experiments/code-v4-would-block-replay.md\n\n================================================================================\nNEW ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA - EACH FAILS ON THE CURRENT TREE\n================================================================================\n  1. pytest tests/unit/test_code_review_criteria_routing.py\n       -> file absent today, so the command errors. Passes after.\n  2. grep -n \"Code-v4 friction replay at 0.54\" \\\n       docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration.md\n       COMMAND RUN, OUTPUT: (no match), exit 1. Passes after.\n       Confirmed the document's current headings are: Per-criterion signals /\n       Precision-first proposal / Block-impact of the proposed thresholds /\n       Adjudicated recommendation / Caveats / Data-hygiene finding.\n  3. routing-vs-document parity assertion (same pytest).\n  4. grep -n \"^_BLOCKING_SET = (\" docs/experiments/replay_code_v4_would_block.py\n       COMMAND RUN, OUTPUT: 45:_BLOCKING_SET = (   exit 0\n       -> must return nothing after; and the script must still exit 0 corpus-free.\n\nDescription trimmed to 7797 bytes for the plan-review admission limit; the\nreview-remediation log that was in the description now lives in this file."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787371285957438001,"uuid":"3b4e93fd-a1de-49c0-8201-b48830bd156f"}